      "rationale": "The check corresponds to the selected local obligation. AppendFuture.Response explicitly requires Error to have returned and grants response validity only on success. pipelineDecode directly consumes that interface, accesses Response, and can call updateLastAppended without consulting Error. Consumer readiness does not waive the method contract: the network producer completes and delivers failed futures as well. Its completion ordering establishes availability, but neither successful completion nor an Error call by this consumer.\n\nThe supplied harness invokes the actual decoder and instruments the same delivered future. Its Error marker is adequate for these sequential synchronous calls; Response records the marker before returning controlled fields. Closing stop during Response cannot interrupt the remaining statements of the selected decoder iteration. Completion through finish synchronizes final inspection. The supplied execution 0288e583f7ef460baad040da271276a9 contains response_access with error_returned=false for all three distinct operation IDs, so the access checker has actual exercised triggers. The failed-progress monitor excludes the successful control and correlates each failed result with its own initial_match. The failed Success=false case remains at zero; the artificial failed Success=true case changes from zero to one. These observations support the two reported local comparisons independently. Go test PASS records successful harness execution, not satisfaction of these external properties.\n\nThe guards provide a meaningful alternative protection: Success=false prevents the measured progress change despite invalid response access. The successful control demonstrates progress in the initialized setup. The match-index oracle is sufficient to witness an effective report for this single nonempty request, although it does not detect every possible report or downstream effect. The controlled failed response is admissible for investigating this explicitly selected interface boundary; its contents are not evidence of a built-in producer execution. No semantic revision is needed for this bounded interpretation.",
